  "articleBody": "You've probably got an FAQ page on your website, which is a great start! But if you're wondering why it's not leading to your business being cited by Google AI Overviews or ChatGPT, it's likely because AI systems look for something a little different than what a typical FAQ page offers. It's not just about having answers; it's about how those answers are structured and presented.\n\nMany businesses treat FAQ pages as a catch-all for various questions, leading to vague or unsupported answers. AI systems, however, crave 'fact density' and clarity. If your answers are long-winded, combine several unrelated intents, or lack directness, AI might struggle to extract the specific piece of information it needs.\n\nAnother common mistake is that FAQ pages often assume a visitor is already on your site and browsing. AI, especially in conversational searches, is trying to pull a single, definitive answer. If your FAQ answers aren't self-contained and clear enough to stand alone, they won't be easily citable.\n\nYour existing website's technical structure can also be a barrier. Heavy CMS themes (like many WordPress or Squarespace sites) can create render-blocking JavaScript or slow load times, making it harder for AI crawlers to efficiently parse and understand your FAQ content. AI prefers lean, static HTML that it can process quickly.\n\nFurthermore, traditional FAQ pages often lack the rich JSON-LD schema that AI systems heavily rely on. This structured data explicitly tells AI what your questions and answers are, what services you offer, and how your business relates to those topics. Without it, AI is left to guess, which reduces your chances of being cited.\n\nFinally, most FAQ pages are just one page on one domain. AI Visibility Solutions creates hundreds of dedicated, schema-dense FAQ and help articles, distributing them as an 'AI Resource Library' on high-trust platforms like GitHub. This decentralized approach gives your content a \"clean data\" bias and inherited domain trust that a single FAQ page can't provide.\n\n**Common Mistakes to Avoid**\n\nDon't let your FAQ page be a missed opportunity. Avoid writing vague or unsupported answers, and don't combine too many unrelated questions on one page. Steer clear of just repeating keywords unnaturally; focus on semantic relevance. Also, don't assume that just having an FAQ means AI can understand it; ensure proper structured data is in place and that your content is easily crawlable.\n\nTo truly get your answers cited by AI, you need an approach built for today's answer engines. AI Visibility Solutions helps small businesses transform their expertise into an AI-ready knowledge base, making sure your answers are not just present but also perfectly understood and cited by AI.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
}